{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"chuffy-arbored-goldfish","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\n`rebar claim` records **no assignee** on the deployed MCP server instead of the configured\n`ticket.default_assignee`. `_config_default_assignee` infers the config root as the TRACKER'S\nPARENT directory — an assumption that holds only when the tracker lives inside the repo.\n\n    # src/rebar/_commands/claim.py:84\n    return config.compose_config(root=os.path.dirname(tracker)).ticket.default_assignee or \"\"\n\nIn a checkout the tracker is `<repo>/.tickets-tracker`, so the parent IS the repo root and\n`rebar.toml` is found. The MCP server sets `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`,\nwhose parent `/var/gerrit/site` contains no `rebar.toml`. The lookup returns `\"\"`, and the claim\nrecords an empty assignee.\n\nThe `except Exception: return \"\"` guard (\"a malformed config must never break a claim\") means\nthis degrades **silently** — no warning, no error, just a ticket with no owner.\n\n## Proven on the live box (2026-08-26, container `compose-mcp-1`)\n\nSame call, two roots:\n\n    CWD = /app\n    compose_config(root=None)                    -> 'joeoakhart@navapbc.com'\n    compose_config(root=dirname(REBAR_TRACKER_DIR)) -> ''\n    tracker_dir(None)                            -> /var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets\n\n    $ ls /var/gerrit/site/rebar.toml   -> No such file or directory\n    $ ls /app/rebar.toml               -> 14163 bytes\n    $ echo $REBAR_DEFAULT_ASSIGNEE     -> <unset>   (env override does not rescue it)\n\nThe env-override path (`REBAR_DEFAULT_ASSIGNEE`, `_config_sources.py:316`) is not set in the mcp\ncompose service, so nothing masks the bad root.\n\n## Why this is the only site\n\n`compose_config(root=os.path.dirname(` appears exactly once in `src/rebar` — this line. Every\nother caller passes a real `repo_root` (`_engine_support/gates.py:154`, `reads.py:118,186,347`,\n`verify_opcert.py:117`). `claim.py` is the outlier, and its own docstring asserts the\nassumption it violates: \"Read from the repo root (the tracker's parent)\".\n\nThe MCP write path supplies no `repo_root` at all (`_mcp_writes.py` has no such reference), so\n`repo_root` is `None` there — and `compose_config(root=None)` resolves correctly from CWD `/app`.\nThat is what makes the fix a deletion rather than an addition.\n\n## Fix\n\nResolve config the way every other caller does — pass `repo_root` through (including `None`)\ninstead of substituting the tracker's parent:\n\n    def _config_default_assignee(repo_root=None) -> str:\n        try:\n            return config.compose_config(root=repo_root).ticket.default_assignee or \"\"\n        except Exception:\n            return \"\"\n\n`repo_root` is already in scope at the call site (`claim.py:175`, same function that computes\n`tracker = config.tracker_dir(repo_root)` at `:154`). In a checkout this resolves the same\n`rebar.toml` as today, so CLI behaviour is unchanged; on the box it finds `/app/rebar.toml`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A claim whose tracker sits OUTSIDE the repo resolves `ticket.default_assignee` from the\n      repo root, not from the tracker's parent.\n- [ ] A claim in an ordinary checkout (tracker inside the repo) resolves the same value it does\n      today — no behaviour change.\n- [ ] An explicit `--assignee` still wins over the default, and an explicit `--assignee \"\"`\n      still clears it (the existing sentinel semantics are untouched).\n- [ ] Regression coverage fails if the root reverts to `os.path.dirname(tracker)`.\n\n## Verification\n\n    .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -k \"default_assignee or claim_assignee\" -q -p no:randomly","id":"8bb4-729e-6745-42d0","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"claim records no assignee when the tracker lives outside the repo: default_assignee is resolved from the tracker's parent"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787796913893231001,"uuid":"71adea18-2c42-49c3-868e-58a426d89e01"}